# Frontend Environment Variables
# Copy to .env.local for local development

# API Base URL (without /api/v1 suffix)
# In development, Vite proxy handles /api -> localhost:8080
# In production (Vercel), set this to your Render API URL
VITE_API_URL=

# Google Maps JavaScript API key (optional). Required for the Draw-on-Map
# geofence editor and the Route map pane. Without it the map panes show a
# setup state and the address/radius + import flows still work.
#
# Where the key comes from (one-time setup, ~5 minutes):
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/ and create or
#      select the project that hosts this app (or a dedicated "fms-maps"
#      project).
#   2. Enable the APIs this key must serve: "Maps JavaScript API",
#      "Places API" (address search), and "Directions API" (route planning).
#      The drawing library ships with Maps JS, but the routes flow also calls
#      Directions, so enable it or route drawing falls back to manual mode.
#   3. Create an API key under Credentials > Create credentials > API key.
#   4. Restrict it: under "Application restrictions" choose HTTP referrers and
#      add your production origin (https://your-app.vercel.app/*) plus
#      http://localhost:5173/* for local dev; under "API restrictions" select
#      only the three APIs above. This prevents the key being used from other
#      sites.
#   5. Copy the key here for local dev, and set the same value as the
#      VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY environment variable in Vercel (Project
#      Settings > Environment Variables, Production + Preview) — it is baked
#      in at build time, so a redeploy is required after changing it.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=